; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; ScreenTable_F131E4 -- 0xF131E4-0xF133E3 is FOUR PARALLEL 32-ENTRY ARRAYS
;                       indexed by one screen-row number, not one table of 128.
;
;   0xF131E4  ScreenTable_F131E4        32 code pointers   read at 0xF10700
;   0xF13264  DspEffect_LoadValueTable        32 code pointers   read at 0xF110EA
;   0xF132E4  ScreenDisplayLists_F132E4 32 DATA pointers   read at 0xF110FA
;   0xF13364  DspEffect_RepairValueTable        32 code pointers   read at 0xF1172A
;
; ⚠⚠ CORRECTED 2026-08-25.  This header used to read "128 32-bit words ...
;   classes it TRANSFER ... the entries are ENTRY POINTS and they seed this
;   block's code walk", with the entry count justified by a chain rule that
;   "stops at the first word that is not an 0x00F0xxxx-0x00F7xxxx address".
;   The chain rule ran straight through three array boundaries because six of
;   the eight edge slots hold the SAME constant, 0x00F42C70.  Entries 64..95 are
;   not entry points at all: they are display-list DATA, and 0xF157A8
;   disassembles as `push SR / retd 0x2640 / db`.
; Evidence, all re-derived by `python3 notes/prom_b_screen_arrays.py` (18 checks):
;   * each of the four bases has EXACTLY ONE reference in the whole three-image
;     set, at the address named beside it above;
;   * in every array, row 0 and row 31 hold that array's own DEFAULT value --
;     0x00F42C70 for the three code arrays, 0x00F157A8 for the data one;
;   * the only indexer of 0xF131E4 (0xF106FE, `4*H + base`, then `jp (XBC)`)
;     takes H from byte[4i+1] of the 4-byte records in 0xF124EC-0xF12F23, whose
;     highest live value over all 654 four-byte records in 0xF124EC-0xF12F23 is
;     0x1E -- ⚠ this 654 is a COUNT OF RECORDS IN prom_b AND HAS NOTHING TO DO
;     with the 654 handler slots of prom_a's dispatch matrix at 0xFF3800, which
;     is a different structure in a different image that happens to have the
;     same size.  It cannot reach index
;     32, let alone 64;
;   * 0xF157A8 is a well-formed interpreter-B opcode-02 record, and
;     notes/gen_prom_b_dsp_value_lists.py walks 176 records from there with no
;     slack (converted below).
; Unknown: what the three code arrays' handlers do -- each is sub_XXXXXX -- and
;          which editor screen each of the 32 rows is.
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
ScreenTable_F131E4:
