; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DL_EffectParamPage -- 0xF14FAC-0xF15023, the DSP EFFECT screen's eight
;   parameter-name rows.  0x78 bytes, which is EXACTLY eight interpreter-B
;   records of fifteen; converted 2026-08-31 from the last `.incbin` of the
;   effect region.
; Run by: DspEffect_LoadParamNames (0xF10FF1), which pushes 0x00F15024 and
;   0x00F14FAC and calls slot T_F42E04.
; Layout: each record draws entry (0x2640+j) of EffectParamNames_F15024 -- 17
;   bytes per entry, which is the row stride that table's own header states --
;   with `swi 7` function 0x20, prom_a's LCD_Svc_20_DrawText8x10.  The eight
;   cursors are 640 apart, and 640 is 16 display lines of AP = 40 bytes, so the
;   rows land at x = 72, y = 74, 90, 106, 122, 138, 154, 170, 186.
; Evidence: the eight source variables are (0x2640)-(0x2647) and they are
;   EXACTLY the eight bytes DspEffect_LoadParamNames writes, at stride 4, out of
;   the per-algorithm descriptor it fetched from EffectParamDescriptors_F12F24.
;   Re-derived by `python3 notes/prom_b_effect_param_map.py --selftest`;
;   write-up in notes/FINDINGS-prom_b-dsp-effect-parameters.md.
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
DL_EffectParamPage:
	dlb_string	var=UI_DrawScratch, mask=0xff, shift=0, svc=LCDSVC_DrawText8x10, table=EffectParamNames_F15024, width=17, x=72, y=74	; var: byte 0 of the eight
	dlb_string	var=UI_DrawScratch+1, mask=0xff, shift=0, svc=LCDSVC_DrawText8x10, table=EffectParamNames_F15024, width=17, x=72, y=90	; var: byte 1 of the eight
	dlb_string	var=UI_DrawScratch+2, mask=0xff, shift=0, svc=LCDSVC_DrawText8x10, table=EffectParamNames_F15024, width=17, x=72, y=106	; var: byte 2 of the eight
	dlb_string	var=UI_DrawScratch+3, mask=0xff, shift=0, svc=LCDSVC_DrawText8x10, table=EffectParamNames_F15024, width=17, x=72, y=122	; var: byte 3 of the eight
	dlb_string	var=UI_DrawScratch+4, mask=0xff, shift=0, svc=LCDSVC_DrawText8x10, table=EffectParamNames_F15024, width=17, x=72, y=138	; var: byte 4 of the eight
	dlb_string	var=UI_DrawScratch+5, mask=0xff, shift=0, svc=LCDSVC_DrawText8x10, table=EffectParamNames_F15024, width=17, x=72, y=154	; var: byte 5 of the eight
	dlb_string	var=UI_DrawScratch+6, mask=0xff, shift=0, svc=LCDSVC_DrawText8x10, table=EffectParamNames_F15024, width=17, x=72, y=170	; var: byte 6 of the eight
	dlb_string	var=UI_DrawScratch+7, mask=0xff, shift=0, svc=LCDSVC_DrawText8x10, table=EffectParamNames_F15024, width=17, x=72, y=186	; var: byte 7 of the eight
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; EffectParamNames_F15024 -- 100 rows of 17 bytes, 0xF15024-0xF156C7:
;   the effect parameter labels (`WET`, `DRIVE`, `EMPHASIS Fc`,
;   `LFO WAVEFORM`, `REVERB TIME`).
; Entry count: 100 = (0xF156C8 - 0xF15024) / 17, exact.
; Evidence: 99 of the 100 rows end in `:`, which is what fixes the
;   width at 17; the run is MAXIMAL (byte before 0x1D); and the
;   end is not a guess -- 0xF156C8 is the `+7` pointer of the
;   eight opcode-02 records at 0xF157A8, which pass 7 as the entry
;   width and a mask of 0x1F, and 0xF156C8 + 32*7 = 0xF157A8, the
;   first byte of the next block.
;   ⚠⚠ CORRECTED 2026-08-25.  This header used to say "113 rows of
;   17 bytes ... 1,924 printable bytes ... and, after them, a units
;   strip", with "where the units strip starts" listed as unknown,
;   and it emitted rows 100..112 plus a 3-byte remainder as more
;   17-byte rows.  They are NOT 17-byte rows: they are the separate
;   32 x 7 table below, and the ROM says so through a record that
;   points at it.  The bytes were always right; the framing was not.
; Which parameter belongs to which effect (ANSWERED 2026-08-31, wave 8 --
;   this line was not updated then): byte 4p of EffectParamDescriptors_F12F24's
;   group for effect k is the ROW here of effect k's parameter p;
;   DspEffect_LoadParamNames copies the eight rows to (0x2640)-(0x2647) for
;   DL_EffectParamPage.  notes/FINDINGS-prom_b-dsp-effect-parameters.md.
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
